-### §container-not-viewport — the shell responds to its own width
+### §viewport-not-container — the shell's layout steps use viewport media queries
+- Since: 2026-10-22
+- Decision: the shell's layout steps use viewport `@media` width queries. `.shell` is no longer a size container.
+- Forbidden: `@container` queries and `container-type` in the shell's layout.
+- Reason: agreed in the team sync on 2026-10-22: not everyone on the team knows container queries, so the team
+  dropped them. Supersedes §container-not-viewport. Accepted risk: the incident from 2026-09-14 can happen again.
+  Inside a split pane narrower than 720px on a wide screen, the shell uses the two-column layout and can clip the sidebar.
+
+### §container-not-viewport — the shell responds to its own width (superseded by §viewport-not-container)
 - Since: 2026-09-15
 - Decision: the shell's layout steps use `@container` queries on `.shell`.
 - Forbidden: switching the shell's layout steps to viewport `@media` width queries (`min-width` / `max-width`).
